  "review_notes": [
    "The italic 'as' (t006) is given to the predicate nominal sar, which stands with no preposition and no object marker on it and is what the supplied word demotes to a role phrase (rules 16, 33); the competing reading marks it added.",
    "'am' is read as the auxiliary of 'am ... come' (the archaic perfect of bo) rather than as a copula for the nominal clause, which is why the explicit pronoun keeps only its 'I'."
